{
 "_source": "Spanish and Portuguese Jews' Congregation, London: List of Tora readings and haftarot, pp. 515-517.",
 "_notes": [
  "Vezot haBerakha: Joshua 1:1-10, confirmed against the source (other Sephardi communities end at 1:9).",
  "Vayyelekh: the Shabbat Shuva haftara, as in the source.",
  "Shabbat Rosh Hodesh: Isaiah 66:1-24 is followed by a repetition of 66:23."
 ],
 "_rules": [
  "When parashiyyot are combined, only the last one's haftara is read.",
  "Mattot, Mase and Devarim (42-44) are the three of the Three Weeks; when Mattot and Mase are read together, Mattot's is read after Pinehas and Mase's on the next Shabbat.",
  "Va'ethannan to Nitsavim (45-51) are the seven of consolation, and Vayyelekh's (52) is read on Shabbat Shuva; none of these, nor the four parashiyyot, give way to Rosh Hodesh or Mahar Hodesh: the first and penultimate verses of Shabbat Rosh Hodesh's haftara, or the first and last of Mahar Hodesh's, are added instead.",
  "Rosh Hodesh on Shabbat and Sunday: the first and last verses of Mahar Hodesh are added to Shabbat Rosh Hodesh's haftara, and 66:23 is not repeated.",
  "Shabbat Hanukka on Rosh Hodesh: Shabbat Hanukka's haftara, then the first and last verses of Shabbat Rosh Hodesh's (and of Mahar Hodesh's on the first of two days of Rosh Hodesh)."
 ],
